title: Who's running for the Congreso?
subtitle: The Spanish General Election is just around the corner
view-if: next_spanish_election_time - time <= 3 and congreso_party_tour_timer <= 0
tags: event
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
    Q.congreso_party_tour_timer = 5;

    Q.party_reaching_out_map = false;
    
    Q.spanish_pm_coalition = [Q.spanish_pm_party];
    Q.spa_caretaker_gov = true;
    Q.spanish_coalition_disp = Q.spanish_pm_party + "<span style=\"font-style:italic;\"> caretaker gov.</span>";

    Q.congreso_party_tour_highlight = [];
    Q.congreso_party_tour_viewed_rest = false;
    Q.congreso_party_tour_viewed_catalonia = false;
    Q.congreso_party_tour_viewed_eh = false;
    Q.congreso_party_tour_viewed_ppcc = false;
    Q.congreso_party_tour_viewed_galicia = false;
    Q.congreso_party_tour_viewed_others = false;
!}
go-to: rest
role: event

@rest
on-arrival: {!
    Q.congreso_party_tour_viewed_rest = true;
    Q.congreso_party_tour_highlight = ["rest"];
!}
go-to: show_map
set-jump: rest_desc

@rest_desc
go-to: choices

With [? if spanish_pm_gender == "m": Presidente?][? if spanish_pm_gender == "f": Presidenta?] [+ spanish_pm +] having dissolved the Congreso, and the Gobierno left with only caretaker powers, the upcoming General Election is all the talk. 

Across Spain many parties are running in every constituency. We can count on the classics, PP and PSOE[? if psc_split: , though the latter will not be running in Catalonia after the split with the PSC?].
[? if not iu_in_up or upyd_congreso_s > 0: There's also the traditional minor [? if not iu_in_up and upyd_congreso_s > 0: parties: UPyD and IU.?][? if iu_in_up and upyd_congreso_s > 0: right party of UPyD.?][? if not iu_in_up and upyd_congreso_s < 1: left party of IU. ?]?]

[? if spa_cs_active: The new liberal right, Cs, will also be running with [+ csspa_leader +] at the forefront.?] Meanwhile, the new left[? if not iu_in_up: , Podemos, will also be striving for a spot. ?][?if iu_in_up: will be running as UP: a broad coalition, uniting Podemos and IU among others. ?][? if spa_mpais_active: [+ mpais_leader +], on the flip side, will be running against the odds with mpais. ?]

[? if vox_active: Last but not least, let's not forget about the renewed far-right, VOX.?]

However there's many other smaller parties running only in their home turfs, including us.

@show_map
new-page: true
go-to: jumpScene

= Who's running for the Congreso?

{!<div id="congreso-party-tour-widget" style="width: 95%; margin: 0 auto;"></div>!}

@choices

-@cat
-@ppcc
-@eh
-@galicia
-@others
-@skip
-@continue

@cat
title: Catalonia
view-if: not congreso_party_tour_viewed_catalonia
on-arrival: {!
    Q.congreso_party_tour_viewed_catalonia = true;
    Q.congreso_party_tour_highlight = ["catalonia"];
!}
go-to: show_map
set-jump: cat_desc

@cat_desc
go-to: choices

Here in **Catalonia**, [? if player_party == "erc": [? if not (jxsi_in_congreso and erc_in_jxsi) and not (erc_in_jxcat): we'll of course be in the fight! ?][? if jxsi_in_congreso and erc_in_jxsi: as agreed, we'll be running in the unprecedented joint coalition of JxSí.?][? if erc_in_jxcat: we'll be standing together as part of our agreed JxCat coalition.?]?][? if player_party == "cup": [? if spa_cup_active: we'll of course be running!?][? if not spa_cup_active: our party will not be running for such a foreign election!?] ERC, on their end, will be [? if erc_in_jxcat: running as part of the JxCat coalition.?][? if erc_in_jxsi and jxsi_in_congreso: running as part of the JxSí coalition.?][? if not erc_in_jxcat and not (erc_in_jxsi and jxsi_in_congreso): running as always.?]?] [? if not (jxsi_in_congreso and not erc_in_jxcat): Besides us, [+ parlament_current_ciu +] will also be fighting for their spot. ?]

[? if spa_fr_active: Since [? if player_party == "cup": we're not running,?][? if player_party != "cup": the CUP is not running,?] it looks like FR will be taking their natural spot. ?][? if spa_cup_active: [? if player_party == "cup": We, as recently ratified, ?][? if player_party != "cup": The CUP will be breaking with its historical party line and ?] will be running. ?][+ parlament_current_icv +], on their end, will be running as part of [? if iu_in_up: UP. ?][? if not iu_in_up: Podemos. ?][? if psc_split: The PSC will, after everything, be running independently. ?][? if unio_split and unio_congreso_catalunya_support > 0: Meanwhile, after their split, UDC will also try to retain their spot. ?][? if pdcat_split and pdcat_congreso_catalunya_support > 0: Meanwhile, after their split, the pdcat will also try to retain their spot. ?]

@ppcc
title: Valencia and the Balearic Islands
view-if: not congreso_party_tour_viewed_ppcc
on-arrival: {!
    Q.congreso_party_tour_viewed_ppcc = true;
    Q.congreso_party_tour_highlight = ["ppcc"];
!}
go-to: show_map
set-jump: ppcc_desc

@ppcc_desc
go-to: choices

In **Valencia**, compromis [? if spa_compromis_active: will be also chasing representation to defend the interests of the Valencian people. ?][? if not spa_compromis_active: will be running as a part of the broad left coalition, within [? if iu_in_up: UP. ?][? if not iu_in_up: Podemos. ?]?]

To the east, in the **Balearic Islands**, MES will [? if spa_mes_active: [? if spa_compromis_active: also ?] be running on its own! ?][? if not spa_mes_active: [? if not spa_compromis_active: also?] be running within [? if iu_in_up: UP. ?][? if not iu_in_up: Podemos. ?]?]

@eh
title: Basque Country and Navarre
view-if: not congreso_party_tour_viewed_eh
on-arrival: {!
    Q.congreso_party_tour_viewed_eh = true;
    Q.congreso_party_tour_highlight = ["eh"];
!}
go-to: show_map
set-jump: eh_desc

@eh_desc
go-to: choices

In the **Basque Country**, the EAJ-PNV will be, as always, present alongside with [? if spa_ehbildu_active: ehbildu.?][? if not spa_ehbildu_active: the alternative civic list of Amaiur.?]

On their end, in **Navarre**, UPN will be running [? if spa_nsuma_formed: alonside the PP and Cs as part of the nsuma coalition.?][? if not spa_nsuma_formed and upn_in_pp: with the PP once again.?][? if not upn_in_pp: this time independently from the PP.?] To their left, [? if spa_ehbildu_active: gbai and ehbildu ?][? if not spa_ehbildu_active: Amaiur?].

# TODO: change the conditions when we manage to fold gbai into amaiur if it is ever reformed.

@galicia
title: Galicia
view-if: not congreso_party_tour_viewed_galicia
on-arrival: {!
    Q.congreso_party_tour_viewed_galicia = true;
    Q.congreso_party_tour_highlight = ["galicia"];
!}
go-to: show_map
set-jump: galicia_desc

@galicia_desc
go-to: choices

In **Galicia**, the BNG will [? if spa_bng_active: be running on their own, to defend their explicitly left-sovereignty stance!?][? if not spa_bng_active: will be joining up efforts with the broad UP coalition.?]

@others
title: Other parties
view-if: not congreso_party_tour_viewed_others
on-arrival: {!
    Q.congreso_party_tour_viewed_others = true;
    Q.congreso_party_tour_highlight =  ["others"];
!}
go-to: show_map
set-jump: others_desc

@others_desc
go-to: choices

In **Asturias**, the fac will [? if spa_foro_active: not be repeating its association with the PP and running on their own. ?][? if not spa_foro_active: be repeating its association with the PP.?]

To their east, **Cantabria** will see the PRC running as their regional party. [? if spa_te_active: And, in**Aragon**, texiste will be representing their very own province in their fight not to be forgotten. ?]

Finally, in the **Canary Islands**, cc-pnc will of course be there to fight for their seats.

@skip
title: Skip to the end of the tour
view-if: not (congreso_party_tour_viewed_galicia and congreso_party_tour_viewed_ppcc and congreso_party_tour_viewed_eh and congreso_party_tour_viewed_catalonia and congreso_party_tour_viewed_rest and congreso_party_tour_viewed_others)
on-arrival: {!
    Q.congreso_party_tour_viewed_rest = true;
    Q.congreso_party_tour_viewed_catalonia = true;
    Q.congreso_party_tour_viewed_eh = true;
    Q.congreso_party_tour_viewed_ppcc = true;
    Q.congreso_party_tour_viewed_galicia = true;
    Q.congreso_party_tour_viewed_others = true;
    Q.congreso_party_tour_highlight = [];
!}
go-to: show_map
set-jump: skip_desc

@skip_desc

Who even needs presentations for the parties that are running? You know that better than whoever is writing these texts anyway.

- @continue

@continue
title: Continue...
view-if: congreso_party_tour_viewed_galicia and congreso_party_tour_viewed_ppcc and congreso_party_tour_viewed_eh and congreso_party_tour_viewed_catalonia and congreso_party_tour_viewed_rest and congreso_party_tour_viewed_others
go-to: post_event